WEBVTT

00:08.360 --> 00:11.690
<b>Can I leave this request to you, then?</b>

00:12.110 --> 00:13.450
<b>Sure thing.</b>

00:14.030 --> 00:15.280
<b>That leaves us with this...</b>

00:16.910 --> 00:20.910
<b>Ctrigall's Menace base? That's one of our former enemies to the north!</b>

00:21.370 --> 00:23.670
<b>Did we really get a ghostwriting request from there?</b>

00:23.670 --> 00:26.710
<b>There's much demand for
Dolls among garrisoned soldiers.</b>

00:27.790 --> 00:30.340
<b>And I <i>have</i> been publicizing CH Postal all over. But...</b>

00:30.340 --> 00:31.550
<b>Is there a problem?</b>

00:32.300 --> 00:35.130
<b>Civil war recently broke out over there.</b>

00:37.050 --> 00:42.020
<b>The radicals want to reignite the War,
and the moderates want to keep things as they are.</b>

00:42.020 --> 00:45.270
<b>Right when they finally had peace again.
I don't even know what to say.</b>

00:45.650 --> 00:49.520
<b>I suppose some people can't live without war.</b>

00:50.570 --> 00:51.530
<b>Yeah.</b>

00:52.030 --> 00:54.030
<b>And the Menace base lies on the front lines of that civil war.</b>

00:54.740 --> 00:58.660
<b>I understand why they'd want to send a letter, but it's too dangerous.</b>

00:58.660 --> 01:00.160
<b>It's a bit unfortunate, though.</b>

01:00.990 --> 01:05.500
<b>That soldier must've asked for a Doll because he had a message to send from the battlefield.</b>

01:06.420 --> 01:10.090
<b>But I can't send one of our Dolls to a war zone.</b>

